Just unlucky.  The probability of finding a book in a statue on level
2n to 2n+1 = (n-1)/(n+10).  On levels 1-3 (n=0,1), there is no chance.
 The Oracle may be between level 5-9.

Thus, on level 5 (n=2), you have a 1/12 chance of a statue giving a
spellbook.  That's 11/12 chance of no spellbook, and for all 8 centaur
statues, (!1/12)^8 = 50% chance of no books at all.

On levels 6-7 (n=3), you have a 2/13 chance of a statue giving a
spellbook, and thus a (11/13)^8 = 26.3% chance of no books.

On levels 8-9 (n=4), you have a 3/14 chance of a statue giving a
spellbook, and thus a (11/14)^8 = 14.5% chance of no books.

Also, there will never be spellbooks in statues of tiny monsters.

In other words, having the Oracle level be on level 6 vs. level 5
practically halves the chance of not getting any books from the
centaur statues.

The only case in which n is not based on the dungeon level on which
the statue was created is if you enter the level for the first time
while carrying the amulet of yendor (ie, you levelported past the
Oracle and finally generated that level on your way out).  In that
case, n is determined based on the depth of the Sanctum level.

Final note:  that's the dungeon level on which the statue was
generated, not the level on which it is broken.  There is nothing to
gain by dragging statues down stairs with you...

